{
  "name": "fly",
  "_about": "A fly -- the housefly (Musca domestica), 7 mm long: a grey thorax with four black stripes down its back and stiff black bristles; the abdomen buff-yellow at the sides, chequered grey on top with a dark stripe down the middle; big red-brown compound eyes nearly meeting on the crown, a silvery face, short antennae with a feathery bristle; a sponge-tipped proboscis folded under the head; black bristly legs with sticky pads; clear wings, the fourth vein bent sharply forward near the tip, held back over the abdomen in a V; behind each the knobbed haltere. Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/flies.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (jointed legs on a walking gait; the wings at rest laid back over the abdomen, swung out and beating in the variant \"flying\").",
